      "questions": {
        "addressed": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "Is the specific requirement of `anchor.statement` present in `item.text`? The requirement is that sc-agent's records define the logger-injection path, and a derivative tool's production code does not use it (only its tests do). Examples of presence: 'plan-anchor's production code uses the default logger; only its tests inject a logger'. Being about the same area, or doing the opposite, is not presence. The anchor is a prohibition; an item that simply never does the forbidden thing but does not say so has not stated it. A bare mention of the topic, or a plan to work on it, without the specific content is no, not unclear.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The requirement is present in the item text, in any wording.",
            "no": "The requirement is absent from the item text.",
            "unclear": "Something resembling the requirement appears, but whether it is the requirement cannot be determined."
          }
        },
        "contradicted": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "Would doing what `item.text` describes violate the requirement that sc-agent's records define the logger-injection path, and a derivative tool's production code does not use it (only its tests do)? Violations look like: a derivative tool (judge-jev, plan-anchor or another) injecting its own logger in production code paths. Omitting the requirement, or describing unrelated work, is not a violation.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "Doing the described work would violate the requirement.",
            "no": "Doing the described work would not violate the requirement.",
            "unclear": "Whether the described work would violate the requirement cannot be told from the text."
          }
        },
        "relevant": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "Is `item.text` about the same subject as `anchor.statement`, namely logger construction or injection in sc-agent or a derivative tool? An item that adds or changes logger construction or injection in sc-agent or a derivative tool is about this subject even if it never mentions the anchor. An item about other components or activities is not. An item that only documents, describes, reviews or plans this subject still touches it. Any change to how a derivative tool's logger is constructed or configured touches this subject.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The item is about logger construction or injection in sc-agent or a derivative tool.",
            "no": "The item is about something else and leaves logger construction or injection in sc-agent or a derivative tool untouched.",
            "unclear": "The item names this area only vaguely, so overlap cannot be decided."
          }
        }
      }
    },
